'' THE __FB_ARG_* FAMILY EXPANDS ITS ARGUMENTS AND RE-SPLITS THEM on top-level commas,
'' which is not the C rule and is the whole point of the family: a macro standing in
'' for a LIST contributes every element of it. Measured, with '#define P 1, 2':
''
''     __FB_ARG_COUNT__( P )                  2      not 1
''     __FB_ARG_COUNT__( P, 9 )               3
''     __FB_ARG_EXTRACT__( 0, P, 9 )          1
''     __FB_ARG_EXTRACT__( 2, P, 9 )          9
''     __FB_ARG_LISTEXPAND__( M, 1, P, 9 )    M(1) M(2) M(9)
''
'' Splitting on the WRITTEN commas first made '__FB_ARG_EXTRACT__( 0, L )' expand to
'' the whole of L and every higher index expand to nothing.
'' TEST: cli
'' ARGS: --dump-ir tests/pp/src/arg-extract.bas
'' EXPECT-EXIT: 0
'' EXPECT-OUT: 0 statements not lowered
'' GOLDEN: expected/arg-extract.out
